y","displayName":"CJ Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Nick Schmaltz scores NHL-best 5th goal and Mammoth beat Devils 5-3","description":"— Nick Schmaltz scored his NHL-best fifth goal of the season, and the Utah Mammoth relied on their proficient power play to beat the New Jersey Devils 5-3 on Tuesday night.","story":"NEWARK, N.J. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114770/nick-schmaltz\">Nick Schmaltz</a> scored his NHL-best fifth goal of the season, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/utah/utah-mammoth\">Utah Mammoth</a> relied on their proficient power play to beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> 5-3 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024857/clayton-keller\">Clayton Keller</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042269/mackenzie-weegar\">MacKenzie Weegar</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899951/lawson-crouse\">Lawson Crouse</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2563036/vincent-trocheck\">Vincent Trocheck</a> also scored for the Mammoth, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024868/mikhail-sergachev\">Mikhail Sergachev</a> had three assists to surpass 300 for his career before leaving the game when <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/mammoth-mikhail-sergachev-2f3d0c42e5287fe971d95983cee13b71\">he took a puck to the back of the helmet</a> late in the second period.\n\n\r\n              Utah went 2 for 4 on the power play and has scored on 8 of 13 opportunities this season with the man advantage, including Keller's goal in the first period and Schmaltz's go-ahead tally midway through the second that made it 3-2.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697446/luke-evangelista\">Luke Evangelista</a> scored twice for New Jersey and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233872/jesper-boqvist\">Jesper Boqvist</a> had the other goal.\n\n\r\n              The Mammoth beat the Devils for the first time, having gone 0-4 in the franchise's previous two seasons.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942065/karel-vejmelka\">Karel Vejmelka</a> stopped 30 shots for Utah, and New Jersey's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5111/jake-allen\">Jake Allen</a> made 26 saves.\n\n\r\n              Sergachev reached 300 assists with his second of the game, on Weegar's goal early in the second period. The 28-year-old Russian defenseman reached the milestone in his 634th NHL game.\n\n\r\n              He also assisted on Schmaltz's goal for his seventh career four-assist game and fourth in his last 32 contests.\n\n\r\n              Schmaltz had two assists, the second on Trocheck's goal that made it 5-3 with 3:08 remaining.\n\n\r\n              New Jersey defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904190/jonas-siegenthaler\">Jonas Siegenthaler</a> left with an injury early in the third period.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Mammoth: At Boston on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Devils: Host Vancouver on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-07T02:17:30Z"}}